    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1964-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Combining the two terms and factoring gives \\[\\left(x-\\frac34\\right)\\left(2x-\\frac54\\right)=0.\\] Hence the roots are \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) and \\(\\frac{5}{8},\\) of which \\(\\frac{5}{8}\\) is smaller.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Factor out the common expression \\(x-\\frac34\\)",
        "The remaining linear factor is \\(2x-\\frac54\\)"
      ],
